1
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Hell wants him. Heaven won't take him. Earth needs him.

2
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Constantine is a fantasy, action, horror film directed by Francis Lawrence.

3
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:15,000
John Constantine has literally been to Hell and back.

4
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:18,000
When he teams up with a policewoman to solve the mysterious suicide of her twin sister, their investigation takes them
through the world of demons and angels that exists beneath the landscape of contemporary Los Angeles.

5
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:21,000
John Constantine, played by Keanu Reeves.

6
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:24,000
Angela Dodson / Isabel Dodson, played by Rachel Weisz.

7
00:42:21,000 --> 00:42:27,000
Chas Kramer, played by Shia LaBeouf.

8
00:48:24,000 --> 00:48:30,000
Midnite, played by Djimon Hounsou.

9
00:54:27,000 --> 00:54:33,000
Beeman, played by Max Baker.

10
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Father Hennessy, played by Pruitt Taylor Vince.

11
01:06:33,000 --> 01:06:39,000
Constantine ( KON-stən-TEEN) is a 2005 American supernatural superhero film directed
by Francis Lawrence, and written by Kevin Brodbin and Frank Cappello.

12
01:12:36,000 --> 01:12:42,000
It is loosely based on the Hellblazer comic book series.

13
01:18:39,000 --> 01:18:45,000
The film stars Keanu Reeves as John Constantine, a cynical exorcist with the ability to perceive and
communicate with half-angels and half-demons in their true forms and to travel between Earth and Hell.

14
01:24:42,000 --> 01:24:48,000
The cast also features Rachel Weisz, Shia LaBeouf, Tilda Swinton, Pruitt
Taylor Vince, Djimon Hounsou, Gavin Rossdale and Peter Stormare.

15
01:30:45,000 --> 01:30:51,000
Constantine was released theatrically in the United States on February 18, 2005, to mixed
reviews, and grossed $231 million on a production budget between $70–100 million.

16
01:36:48,000 --> 01:36:54,000
Since its release, it has garnered a cult following.

17
01:42:51,000 --> 01:42:57,000
A sequel is in development.

18
01:48:54,000 --> 01:49:00,000
The film explores themes of self sacrifice, angel,
christianity, confession, superhero.

19
01:54:57,000 --> 01:55:03,000
The tone is dark.
